{"id":"f69b1c52c2ce36a83bfcf538ad47ef4740139de9","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"f69b1c52c2ce36a83bfcf538ad47ef4740139de9","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/store-prune-frozen-store.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@","+---","+\"@pnpm/store.commands\": patch","+\"pnpm\": patch","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm store prune` now fails with `ERR_PNPM_FROZEN_STORE_WRITE` when `frozenStore` is enabled. It used to remove files from the store."],"additions":7,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":".changeset/store-prune-python-wheels.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm store prune` no longer removes files of the wheels that an installed Python project uses, so `pnpm install --offline` can recreate its environment. Pruning now also removes the store index entries of Python and Cargo archives whose files it deleted."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/store.rs","lines":["@@ -18,8 +18,13 @@ use clap::{","     Args,","     Subcommand,"," };","+use derive_more::{","+    Display,","+    Error,","+};"," use miette::{","     Context,","+    Diagnostic,","     IntoDiagnostic,"," };"," use pnpm_config::{","@@ -78,7 +83,17 @@ impl StoreCommand {","     }"," }"," ","+/// `pnpm store prune` asked to remove files from a store `frozenStore`","+/// keeps read-only.","+#[derive(Debug, Display, Error, Diagnostic)]","+#[display(\"Cannot prune the store because frozenStore is enabled (the store is opened read-only)\")]","+#[diagnostic(code(ERR_PNPM_FROZEN_STORE_WRITE), help(\"Turn off frozenStore to prune the store.\"))]","+pub struct FrozenStorePruneError;","+"," fn prune(config: &Config) -> miette::Result<()> {","+    if config.frozen_store {","+        return Err(FrozenStorePruneError.into());","+    }","     // The dlx cache holds hard links into the store, so it is","     // cleaned first to let this prune reclaim what the expired","     // entries used."],"additions":15,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/src/cli_args/store/in_use_files.rs","lines":["@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@"," //! keep it. A package linked from a modules directory not named"," //! `node_modules` is found only through the projects that the installed"," //! lockfiles list.","+//!","+//! A Python environment rewrites each wheel's `RECORD`, so that store file","+//! has no hard link either while the wheel's other files do."," "," use pnpm_config::{","     Host,","@@ -25,7 +28,6 @@ use pnpm_lockfile::{"," use pnpm_modules_yaml::read_modules_layout;"," use pnpm_package_manifest::safe_read_project_manifest_from_dir;"," use pnpm_store_dir::{","-    CafsFileInfo,","     InUse,","     PackageFilesIndex,","     PruneError,","@@ -55,6 +57,9 @@ use std::{"," ///   of every side-effects entry;"," /// - the modules directory of every project it lists."," ///","+/// Every file of the rows of the archives each registered project's","+/// `pylock.toml` pins.","+///"," /// A project without a current lockfile, a project whose lockfile version"," /// this pnpm does not support, and a package without a row add no files. A"," /// registry error keeps its own code, and any other failure is","@@ -66,6 +71,7 @@ pub(super) fn in_use(store_dir: &StoreDir) -> Result<InUse, PruneError> {","         // The registry joins a relative link target without normalizing it.","         let project = lexical_normalize(&project);","         let modules_dir = modules_dirs.add(&project).map_err(PruneError::InUseFiles)?;","+        keys.extend(python_index_keys(&project).map_err(PruneError::InUseFiles)?);","         for lockfile in","             load_installed_lockfiles(&project, &modules_dir).map_err(PruneError::InUseFiles)?","         {","@@ -95,7 +101,7 @@ fn in_use_files(","         read_rows(store_dir, &keys).map_err(io::Error::other).map_err(PruneError::InUseFiles)?;","     Ok(rows","         .iter()","-        .flat_map(row_files)","+        .flat_map(PackageFilesIndex::all_files)","     